27s_Church,_Owthorpe","cat":"St Margaret's Church, Owthorpe","stories":[{"layer":"people","text":"John Hutchinson, born at Owthorpe in 1615, held Nottingham Castle for Parliament from 1643 and signed Charles I's death warrant.[^s1] He died a prisoner in 1664 and is buried at Owthorpe; his wife Lucy's Memoirs of his life made him famous.[^s1]","source":{"title":"John Hutchinson (Roundhead)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hutchinson_(Roundhead)","kind":"Wikipedia"},"who":"John Hutchinson","sources":[{"title":"Owthorpe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owthorpe","kind":"Wikipedia"}],"cites":{"s1":{"title":"John Hutchinson (Roundhead)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hutchinson_(Roundhead)","kind":"Wikipedia"}},"weblinks":[["his wife Lucy","note:Lucy Hutchinson"]],"links":["Lucy Hutchinson"],"own":1}],"sum":"St Margaret's Church, Owthorpe is a Grade II* listed parish church in the Church of England in Owthorpe, Nottinghamshire, England. Owthorpe has an unusual Grade II* listed Anglican church, dedicated to St Margaret of Antioch, once considered a patron saint of pregnancy. It stands away from the village in farmland, surrounded by a low wall, next to the site where the manor stood.","sumSrc":{"title":"St Margaret's Church, Owthorpe","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Margaret%27s_Church%2C_Owthorpe"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","coll":[{"title":"Nottingham Castle","url":"https://picturenottingham.co.uk/image-themes/nottingham-castle.html"}],"xy":[-1.00217,52.89423]},"320959":{"h":10,"osm":"way/229250612","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Church_Barn%2C_Owthorpe_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5207885.jpg","credit":{"file":"Church Barn, Owthorpe - geograph.org.uk - 5207885.jpg","year":2016,"author":"Jonathan Thacker","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0"},"council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council","xy":[-1.00326,52.89413]},"320960":{"h":10,"osm":"way/229250611","kind":"barn","council":"Rushcliffe Borough Council",